[?2004l[?2004h>     Optimized reference model: out = (1 + scaling) * (x @ W^T + b)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h>     The (1 + scaling) factor is folded into precomputed weights/bias.
[?2004l[?2004h>     The GEMM runs on fp16 tensor cores with error compensation
[?2004l[?2004h>     (Ootomo-style split): each fp32 operand is split as hi + lo fp16,
[?2004l[?2004h>     and out ~= xh@Wh + xh@Wl + xl@Wh accumulated in fp32.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h>     The fp16 weight halves are stored as int16 bit-views so that a
[?2004l[?2004h>     Module.to(dtype=torch.float32) call by the evaluator does not alter them.
[?2004l[?2004h>     """
